<BaseLayout title="Partner disclosure — Yeast Travel" description="How Yeast Travel labels affiliate links and partner experiences.">
  <article class="legal shell"><span class="eyebrow">Commercial transparency</span><h1>If we earn,<br/>you’ll see why.</h1><section><h2>Affiliate link</h2><p>When a booking link can earn Yeast a commission, the page will say <strong>Affiliate link</strong>. The traveller pays and contracts with the named platform or supplier, not Yeast.</p></section><section><h2>Partner experience</h2><p>A paid activity fulfilled by another operator will say <strong>Partner experience</strong> and name the fulfiller, language, price range, cancellation rule and qualification status.</p></section><section><h2>Neutral routes</h2><p>Free itinerary order is not sold to merchants. A café, shop or market is never required merely because it could pay a commission.</p></section><section><h2>Current status</h2><p>No external paid offer is published in this research-preview build. Shanghai Side Quest is marked Coming soon and has no purchase action.</p></section></article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.legal{max-width:820px;padding-block:70px}.legal h1{margin:25px 0 65px;font-family:var(--display);font-size:clamp(58px,9vw,105px);font-weight:400;line-height:.88;letter-spacing:-.06em}.legal section{padding:25px 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.legal h2{font-family:var(--display);font-size:31px;font-weight:400}.legal p{color:var(--muted)}</style>
